{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401119-cults-of-the-blood-gods-the-youtube-chronicle","id":1401119,"title":"Cults of the Blood Gods: the YouTube chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-05T07:56:00-07:00","id":1401119,"title":"Cults of the Blood Gods: the YouTube chronicle","content":"So... I just finished watching <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E_VtuU4y9JI&amp;t=11s\" target=\"_blank\">this show</a> from Red Moon Roleplaying.<br /> <br /> I enjoyed it as a viewer as it was well acted, while the players and the Storyteller kept true to their characters and NPCs.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller there are some things that left me cold though. Without entering spoiler territory I think there are some big plot holes and I don't agree with how some of the scenes were set up (in an unfair way to the PCs imo). There were mistakes from the PCs for sure and I also think some of what happened was done so in order to provide a better &quot;cinematographic experience&quot; to the viewers. Even so I found myself wondering because the way the game was run (rules aside) is quite distant from the way I run things.<br /> <br /> So, in short: have you seen this series and what do you think of it as players and Storytellers? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T15:33:40-07:00","id":1401205,"title":"","content":"Come on! Did anyone see this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T15:36:06-07:00","id":1401207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401119-cults-of-the-blood-gods-the-youtube-chronicle?p=1401205#post1401205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come on! Did anyone see this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen about half. I actually did a TV tropes page for its sister series in THE SACRIFICE.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/WebVideo/ChicagoByNightTheSacrifice\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...htTheSacrifice</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T16:03:18-07:00","id":1401211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401119-cults-of-the-blood-gods-the-youtube-chronicle#post1401119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I just finished watching <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E_VtuU4y9JI&amp;t=11s&amp;quot;]this</a> show[/URL] from Red Moon Roleplaying.<br /> <br /> I enjoyed it as a viewer as it was well acted, while the players and the Storyteller kept true to their characters and NPCs.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller there are some things that left me cold though. Without entering spoiler territory I think there are some big plot holes and I don't agree with how some of the scenes were set up (in an unfair way to the PCs imo). There were mistakes from the PCs for sure and I also think some of what happened was done so in order to provide a better &amp;quot;cinematographic experience&amp;quot; to the viewers. Even so I found myself wondering because the way the game was run (rules aside) is quite distant from the way I run things.<br /> <br /> So, in short: have you seen this series and what do you think of it as players and Storytellers? </div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that we cut a lot of the dice rolling out of the edited show, so it's more entertaining to listen to. What might seem unfair to you, the listener, is something that was determined off mic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T19:33:54-07:00","id":1401254,"title":"","content":"I have only listened to the first couple of episodes so far. I find the play style, alongside The Sacrifice, emphasizes personal tragedy. Fits nicely into the &quot;game of personal and political horror&quot; of V5. It is, in tone, very different from LA by Night. I enjoy both very much but I find I need breaks when listening to the Sacrifice or CotBG. I am wimp when it comes to horror and suspense stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T16:25:44-07:00","id":1404315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401119-cults-of-the-blood-gods-the-youtube-chronicle?p=1401211#post1401211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind that we cut a lot of the dice rolling out of the edited show, so it's more entertaining to listen to. What might seem unfair to you, the listener, is something that was determined off mic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duly noted. Still there were things that did not convince me that had nothing to do with rolls.<br /> <br /> -Neonates being sent to scout an abandoned Giovanni domain with no help and no resources. I get you wanted to represent the Giovanni family as uncaring but sending 4 neonates into a suicide mission of sorts seems a just like a mismanagement of resources AND a political mishap. These neonates have sires (or adoptive sires) and a couple of them come from powerful families from Boston. Sending them to their deaths hardly seems wise even if Donatello Giovanni doesn't really care about them.<br /> -No one asking about who the potential mole could be. Who are the people who could know about the Promise of 1528? Three out of four PCs did not know about it for example. Giving the content of what was leaked it was immediately clear the mole was a member of the family so asking Donatello who the members of the Hecata in Atlantic City were should have been a given, or Donatello himself volunteering the information for that matter.<br /> -Admittedly the players did make a lot of mistakes. The first person they meet in Atlantic City is a ghoul who used to be a Giovanni pawn but now drinks from another vampire and they think that can fly? He's managing Giovanni assets while having a regnant from a different clan. That alone should have put them on their guard instead they kept considering the hotel where they were staying as secure. I can honestly say my usual bunch of players would have never (ever) made that mistake.<br /> -The way Jason Carl's character died came across as staged or extremely unfair. It stands to reason it could happen of course, but judging from the the way was represented &quot;on screen&quot; he did not have a chance to realize the danger until it was too late and he walked into his own death.<br /> -What happened with Maria when she was kidnapped. Mistakes from the players aside (staying in that hotel and sleeping in different rooms after one of them was just killed?) the odds seemed stacked way too much against her suceeding (3 vs 1 by day with corresponding dice penalty and she's the only one who gets kidnapped so the coterie is effectively split again without a chance for players to make that choice?)<br /> -&quot;John Smith&quot; calling back HQ in New York after the murder and being told to get rid of the opposition when it was clear he and what was left of the coterie were just a bunch of neonates left on their own deep into hostile territory.<br /> -I was going to say no insight rolls against the laying toreador ghoul managing the Giovanni's hotel but given the fact you did not include all of your rolls you probably gave them those checks and they failed them.<br /> -The cover up story. Sammie G was in good standing with the family. The moment &quot;John Smith&quot; goes back to NY and tells his story he should get checked with dominate or auspex. And then he's screwed. That aside, Moulbrey would probably want to know what happened to Natalie, same thing with the Lamiae of Boston and the Milliners for Raymond. John should know that by going back he's got a lot of explaining to do and he doesn't seem equipped for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}